.fullchain 

# ⚑ BUILT WASM ENGINES ARE REGENERATED, NEVER KEPT.
#
# On 2026-08-01 three untracked engine trees were found shipping alongside the source:
# `portal/dist/pkg` (a 2026-07-02 PRE-IMT engine, which is why a stale 6-arg call in
# `portal/dist/cell.html` looked locally consistent), `site/dist` (Jul-27, refused BOTH the old and
# the new envelope), and `wasm/pkg-mwt` (Jul-14, pre-IMT). 311 MB of verifiers that could not be
# right, none of them tracked, none of them regenerated when the engine changed.
#
# ⚠ The failure mode is specific: an untracked built artifact makes a STALE CALLER look correct,
# because the caller and the engine were stale together. `289720ca8` (Jul 26) identified one of these
# blobs by name and nothing regenerated it for five days.
#
# Rebuild: site/dist -> scripts/build-pages-dist.sh · portal/dist/pkg, wasm/pkg* -> build.sh wasm
site/dist/
wasm/pkg-mwt/

# ⚑ An ORPHANED worktree directory inside the repo root. `git worktree list` no longer
# names it, but 4571 `.rs` files remain on disk — so every gate that walks the FILESYSTEM
# (rather than `git ls-files`) scanned the whole repo TWICE through it. Measured 2026-08-07:
# `check-bare-ignore` reported 556 `#[ignore]`s against a real 270; 43 of its 45 fence
# findings were headver echoes of BASELINED rows (the baseline keys on repo-relative paths,
# so it can never match them); 1017 of 5483 `check-production-callers` lines and 33 of 58
# `check-silent-skip` rows were the same echo.
#
# ⚠ Ignoring it stops the double-scan. DELETING it is whoever created it's call.
headver/
